  'akidah_1.1': <ArticleBlock>[
    Heading('Why Believe in God at All?'),
    Paragraph('Okay — before we talk about prayer, fasting, or any other worship, we need to answer the most basic question first: "Is there even a God?"'),
    Paragraph('That\'s a totally fair question. It\'s actually a good thing to think about, because it means you\'re serious about finding the truth. Let\'s walk through it with simple logic.'),
    Subheading('🔍 Argument 1: The Design of the Universe'),
    Paragraph('Look around you. The phone you\'re holding — screen, processor, camera, battery. That advanced. But you know for sure SOMEONE designed it, right? Those parts couldn\'t just pop out of nothing.'),
    Paragraph('Now imagine: the universe is FAR more complex than a phone. Trillions of galaxies, each with billions of stars. Gravity, the speed of light, the water cycle, photosynthesis — all working with insane precision. If a phone needs a designer, how could something far more advanced just happen by accident?'),
    Highlight('Even a phone needs a designer. The universe? Far more complex.'),
    Subheading('⛓️ Argument 2: Cause and Effect'),
    Paragraph('Here\'s the most basic law of the world: everything has a cause. A table exists because someone built it. A tree grows because a seed was planted. You exist because you have parents.'),
    Paragraph('Keep tracing it backwards — who made X, who made Y — and you must stop at one point: something that does NOT need a cause. Something that already existed from the beginning. That\'s what we call God.'),
    Paragraph('Think of a chain: if every link depends on the one before it, who connected the first link? There must be something that isn\'t a link, but is the source of all the links.'),
    Subheading('🎯 Argument 3: This Order Can\'t Be Coincidence'),
    Paragraph('Flip a coin 100 times. How often would you get heads every single time? Nearly impossible. Now imagine: the universe has LAWS that have worked consistently for billions of years. Gravity never takes a day off. Atoms never act randomly. The day-night cycle never runs late.'),
    Paragraph('Order this extreme without a Designer? That\'s like saying a finished novel popped out of an explosion at a printing shop. It doesn\'t add up.'),
