    Paragraph('Okay — in the last module we established there\'s a Designer behind the universe. Next question: "Is there really only one? Couldn\'t there be more?"'),
    Paragraph('This question matters a lot, because the answer shapes how we see the entire universe. Let\'s work through it with the same simple logic — relaxed, no overcomplicating.'),
    Subheading('🚗 Analogy: Two Drivers, One Steering Wheel'),
    Paragraph('Imagine you\'re in a car. Suddenly TWO people grab the steering wheel. One wants to turn left, the other right. What happens? A crash. Chaos. Nobody arrives anywhere.'),
    Paragraph('Now picture the universe. Millions of physical laws operating together with super precision — gravity, electromagnetism, strong and weak nuclear forces. They all complement each other and never conflict.'),
    Paragraph('If there were TWO "gods" with different wills, there would be a collision somewhere. One wants gravity stronger, the other weaker. One wants water to flow down, the other up. The result? Chaos.'),
    Highlight('But reality: the universe is incredibly tidy. Consistent for billions of years. That\'s only possible if there is ONE source of will.'),
    Subheading('🔬 Evidence from Cosmic Order'),
