  'praktik_3.2': <ArticleBlock>[
    Heading('Conditions of Validity & Pillars of Prayer'),
    Paragraph('Before entering the prayer sequence, you need to understand two things that often confuse beginners: validity conditions and pillars. They sound similar, but they differ.'),
    Subheading('📋 Conditions of Validity'),
    Paragraph('Validity conditions are things that must be fulfilled BEFORE the prayer. If unmet, the prayer is invalid no matter how perfect the movements. There are 5:'),
    Paragraph('① Islam — the performer is a Muslim.'),
    Paragraph('② Free from minor impurity — handled by wudhu, covered in the previous module.'),
    Paragraph('③ Covering the aurat — for men: navel to knees. For women: the whole body except face and palms. Wear clothing that\'s neither see-through nor tight.'),
    Paragraph('④ Facing the Qibla — the direction toward the Ka\'bah in Makkah. From Indonesia, it\'s westward angled slightly north (northwest). If unsure, use the app\'s Qibla feature in the Schedule tab.'),
    Paragraph('⑤ The prayer time has entered — each prayer has a specific window. Fajr before sunrise, Dhuhr after the sun declines westward, and so on. Praying outside the window = invalid.'),
    Highlight('Validity conditions = things OUTSIDE the prayer that must be done first. Miss one? The prayer is void from the start.'),
    Subheading('🧱 Pillars of Prayer'),
    Paragraph('Pillars are things performed WITHIN the prayer. Missing one makes the prayer invalid. There are 13 pillars (some scholars say 14):'),
    Paragraph('① Intention in the heart, at the moment of takbiratul ihram.'),
    Paragraph('② Takbiratul ihram — saying "Allahu Akbar" while raising the hands. This marks the prayer\'s start.'),
    Paragraph('③ Standing (qiyam) — upright during the prayer.'),
    Paragraph('④ Reciting Al-Fatihah — obligatory in every rakaat, whether leading (imam) or alone.'),
    Paragraph('⑤ Ruku — bowing, hands gripping the knees, back straight.'),
    Paragraph('⑥ I\'tidal — rising from ruku, standing upright.'),
    Paragraph('⑦ Sujud — two prostrations in each rakaat.'),
    Paragraph('⑧ Sitting between the two prostrations — sitting briefly after the first sujud, before the second.'),
    Paragraph('⑨ The final tasyahud — sitting at the last rakaat and reciting tasyahud.'),
    Paragraph('⑩ Reciting salawat upon Prophet Muhammad ﷺ within the final tasyahud.'),
    Paragraph('⑪ Sitting for the final (and first) tasyahud — the iftirasy position: left foot tucked beneath, right upright.'),
    Paragraph('⑫ Reciting the two sentences of shahada within the final tasyahud.'),
    Paragraph('⑬ Turning in salam — "Assalamu alaikum warahmatullah" to the right, then left. This ends the prayer.'),
    Paragraph('⑭ In order (tertib) — performing all pillars in sequence.'),
    Highlight('Validity conditions = BEFORE prayer. Pillars = WITHIN the prayer. The difference: validity conditions make the prayer ALLOWED to begin; pillars make it BECOME valid.'),
    Subheading('💡 Why Need This?'),
    Paragraph('Because many beginners ask: "Is my prayer valid?" If the validity conditions are met and the pillars complete — your prayer is valid. Simple. No need to overthink.'),
    Cta('Got the conditions and pillars? Take the quiz, then continue to praying step-by-step! 🎯'),
  ],
