    Paragraph('• Tawaf — circling the Ka\'bah 7 times. Life must be centered on Allah, like planets orbiting.'),
    Paragraph('• Wukuf at Arafah — a reminder of the Day of Judgment, when all humans gather on the plain of mahsyar.'),
    Paragraph('• Stoning the jumrah — symbolizing rejection of Satan\'s temptations, from the small to the great.'),
    Subheading('💰 The Obligatory Conditions of Hajj'),
    Paragraph('Hajj is only obligatory if you\'re ABLE. Meaning:'),
    Paragraph('• Physically healthy — able to walk, stand, and endure hot weather. If seriously ill, it isn\'t obligatory.'),
    Paragraph('• Financially sufficient — with travel costs AND the family back home still provided for. You mustn\'t go to hajj while debt piles up.'),
    Paragraph('• The journey is safe — the route to Makkah must be safe.'),
    Highlight('Hajj is obligatory if able. If not yet able, there\'s no sin. Allah doesn\'t burden anyone beyond their capacity.'),
    Subheading('💡 Closing of the Pillars of Islam Category'),
    Paragraph('These five pillars — Shahada, Salat, Fasting, Zakat, Hajj — are the FOUNDATION of a Muslim\'s life. Each fills a different aspect: heart, time, desires, wealth, and body.'),
    Paragraph('If you understand \'Aqidah and the Pillars of Islam, you already hold a strong framework. Now it\'s time to move into the practical part.'),
    Cta('Pillars of Islam category complete! 🎉 Continue to the "Worship Practice" tab to learn how to pray from zero. You\'re getting better! 🚀'),
